testdata/optional_widening/cast.a:3:15: Adamic 0.1 refuses an unproven relation from { x: number; } to { x: number; y?: number; }: optional field y has no proven compatible presence/type; keep compatible optional fields in both views, or construct an object with explicitly compatible fields (adamic/no-optional-widening); use a proven upcast, cast a discriminated object union with unique literal or enum tags to members or a sub-union, or downcast along nominal class ancestry (adamic/no-unchecked-cast)
